/-!
# Amplification for Original Static Oracles

This module combines `originalStaticOuterWord` with randomized amplitude amplification for a
target approximated by a finite linear combination of the evolutions generated by `H + s j • L`.
The input is an exact block encoding of `L + Complex.I • H`, together with a preparation
unitary, a computational success projector, and a positive lower bound on the target output
norm.

`originalA_static_amplified_target` supplies a well-formed oracle word, a heralding probability
of at least one eighth, exact expected input and data query counts, and a normalized output
approximation up to a unit complex phase. Its error combines the weighted sample approximation
error with the supplied analytic discrepancy. See [WangEtAl2026].

## Main statements

* `OriginalStaticSpace` names the workspace used by the static oracle and amplification
  circuits.
* `originalA_static_amplified_target` packages the amplified preparation, query bounds, and
  conditional output guarantee.

## References

* [Wang et al., 2026][WangEtAl2026]
-/

set_option warningAsError false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false

